2c:["$","h2","3",{"children":"When building makes sense"}]
2d:["$","ul","4",{"children":[["$","li","The process is a real point of difference, and a generic tool would flatten it.",{"children":"The process is a real point of difference, and a generic tool would flatten it."}],["$","li","You are paying for several products and stitching them together by hand every day.",{"children":"You are paying for several products and stitching them together by hand every day."}],["$","li","Licence costs scale with users or volume in a way that will soon exceed the cost of ownership.",{"children":"Licence costs scale with users or volume in a way that will soon exceed the cost of ownership."}],["$","li","You need integration or control that available products do not offer.",{"children":"You need integration or control that available products do not offer."}]]}]
2e:["$","h2","5",{"children":"The option people forget"}]
2f:["$","p","6",{"children":"It is rarely all or nothing. A common and sensible pattern is to buy the commodity parts and build only the piece that is specific to you, connecting the two through APIs. You get a maintained foundation and a custom layer small enough to own comfortably."}]
30:["$","h2","7",{"children":"Count the whole cost"}]
31:["$","p","8",{"children":"Compare the options over several years, not at the point of purchase. For a product, include licences, configuration, training and the manual work it leaves behind. For custom software, include hosting, maintenance and the changes you will inevitably want. An honest comparison often settles the argument."}]
